{"Title":"An Act relative to prescription opioid abuse prevention education","BillNumber":"S333","DocketNumber":"SD1567","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"PrimarySponsor":{"Id":"JRO0","Name":"Jacob R. Oliveira","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JRO0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T17:51:44.94"},"Cosponsors":[{"Id":"JRO0","Name":"Jacob R. Oliveira","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/JRO0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-19T17:51:44.94"},{"Id":"SND0","Name":"Sal N. DiDomenico","Type":1,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/LegislativeMembers/SND0","ResponseDate":"2023-01-30T09:38:54.1133333"}],"JointSponsor":null,"BillHistory":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Documents/S333/DocumentHistoryActions","LegislationTypeName":"Bill","Pinslip":"By Mr. Oliveira, a petition (accompanied by bill, Senate, No. 333) of Jacob R. Oliveira and Sal N. DiDomenico for legislation relative to prescription opioid abuse prevention education.  Education.","DocumentText":"\tSection 1 of chapter 71 of the general laws, as so appearing in the 2020 edition, is hereby amended by inserting after the word “violence”, in line 22, the following words:- “, prescription opioid abuse prevention, with an emphasis on the prescription drug epidemic and the connection between prescription opioid abuse and addiction to other drugs, such as heroin,”.\r\n","EmergencyPreamble":null,"RollCalls":[],"Attachments":[],"CommitteeRecommendations":[{"Action":"Accompanied","FiscalAmounts":[],"Committee":{"CommitteeCode":"J14","GeneralCourtNumber":193,"Details":"https://malegislature.gov/api/GeneralCourts/193/Committees/J14"},"Votes":[]}],"Amendments":[]}